                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Cranky Cat is a puzzle game based around rotating a wheel (or \"crank\") and matching 3+ colours to make balloons pop. \n\nThe game itself works okay, but the concept, after 24 levels over 5 stages (120 odd levels) gets boring and trite. The worst part, however, is the soundtrack, which literally consists of 3-4 tracks which they play over... and over... and over... and over again. Incredibly annoying, I had to turn the volume to 0% just to ignore it.\n\nIt took me 5 hours to complete the Story mode entirely. I looked at the puzzles, they seemed pretty easy but they looked more entertaining than the Story mode.\n\nThis game would suit people who \"like these sorts of games\", people who enjoy Bejeweled, Peggled, Tetris etc, parents who don't play games often will possibly enjoy the simple puzzlesolving aspect, but may be driven genuinely insane by the \"soundtrack\".\n\nNilesy",
